X pixmaps as the web process's render target (GTK 3 on X11, opt-in)

Without DMA-BUF, the web process renders each frame into a renderbuffer, reads it back with
glReadPixels into shared memory, and the UI process uploads that to X through cairo: ~24 MB of
memory traffic a frame on the OzoneHD box (Mali-450, 32-bit DDR3), ~25 frames a second at most.

With WEBKIT_X11_PIXMAP_RENDERER=1 the swap chain's buffers are X pixmaps instead: the GPU renders
into a texture on each one's EGLImage (top down, so no mirroring), the UI process gets the XID
and composites the pixmap with XRender, inside X. No CPU copy of the frame in either process.
